WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Recap: Structure, Governance & Accountability

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Check that your structure, decisions and accountability fit together before your first hire.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
You designed the work before the job titles: who will do what, who decides what, how governance stays separate from management, and how accountability and coordination work from day one.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:36.659
3.1 From work to structure: Structure follows the work: it starts from the capabilities your strategy needs, including work not yet started.

6
00:00:36.659 --> 00:00:46.407
3.2 Organisational structures and organigrams: An organigram shows roles and reporting lines; most new organisations start functional or as a small hub.

7
00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:57.156
3.3 Governance structures by legal form: Governance directs and holds to account; management runs the daily work. Both exist from day one.

8
00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:58.156
One lesson at a time

9
00:00:58.156 --> 00:01:07.904
3.4 Board and management responsibilities: The board sets direction and oversees; management proposes and runs. Founders do both until a board exists.

10
00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:18.022
3.5 Roles and role descriptions: A role card sets out purpose, results and authority; founders need one too, as their roles blur first.

11
00:01:18.022 --> 00:01:29.511
3.6 Decision rights and delegation of authority: A delegation of authority states who may approve what, up to which limit, before the first contract.

12
00:01:29.911 --> 00:01:30.511
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:30.511 --> 00:01:40.630
3.7 RACI and process ownership: RACI makes who does what explicit, which helps even two co-founders who tend to assume rather than ask.

14
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:50.007
3.8 Accountability and reporting lines: Accountability runs upward, sideways and downward, and starts with the people you serve and first supporters.

15
00:01:50.007 --> 00:02:01.126
3.9 Coordination and internal communication: A reliable hand-off needs a named recipient, an agreed output and a date, not just a shared document.

16
00:02:01.726 --> 00:02:15.067
Your structure and role cards are the starting point for your people plan: how many people you need, with what skills, from when, and how you will support them.

17
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:20.467
You check your Structure & Accountability Pack and download each exercise as a PDF.

18
00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:25.067
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
